SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bangkok votes in new governor for first time in nine years","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters reporting)","publication_date":"2022-05-23","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/05/23/us-thailand-politics-bangkok","claim":"Chadchart Sittipunt won Bangkok's first governor election in nine years by a wide margin, which Reuters framed as a sign of waning popularity for Prayuth and a somewhat more open political environment for opposition challengers.","locator":"lines 658-665","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire reporting on contemporaneous election results with explicit result figures and attribution to the Election Commission.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 local-election evidence within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant: it reflects the political climate under Prayuth's government, not a personal act by him.","contrary_evidence":["A Bangkok governor race is local, not a national transfer-of-power test.","The result does not by itself prove systemic democratization at the national level."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Explainer-How a Thai court suspended Prime Minister Prayuth","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters reporting)","publication_date":"2022-08-25","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/08/25/thailand-politics-suspension","claim":"Thailand's Constitutional Court suspended Prayuth while considering an eight-year term-limit petition; Reuters called it a rare victory for opposition parties, and the article notes the term-limit rule sits in the 2017 constitution written by a military-appointed committee after the coup.","locator":"lines 642-647","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters contemporaneous explanation of the court action, the constitutional basis, and the opposition's strategy.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 evidence on term-limit contestation and constitutional structure.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Prayuth as incumbent PM; the source is about his hold on office and the rules around it, not his voluntary restraint.","contrary_evidence":["The suspension was temporary and did not end his tenure.","This is judicial constraint, not evidence that Prayuth himself respected term limits."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.8","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Constitutional Court rules Prayut can stay on as PM","publisher":"Nation Thailand","publication_date":"2022-09-30","url":"https://www.nationthailand.com/thailand/politics/40020589","claim":"The Constitutional Court ruled 6:3 that Prayuth had not exceeded the constitutionally permitted eight-year term because the clock counted from April 6, 2017, allowing him to continue in office.","locator":"lines 23-26","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Local reporting of the final verdict with the vote split and the court's legal interpretation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 evidence within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Prayuth: it concerns his tenure and how the constitutional rule was applied to him.","contrary_evidence":["The ruling preserved incumbent continuity rather than demonstrating democratic transfer.","It does not show a voluntary commitment by Prayuth to abide by term limits."],"lenses":["4B.8","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Thailand","publisher":"Reuters Institute for the Study of Journalism","publication_date":"2022-06-15","url":"https://reutersinstitute.politics.ox.ac.uk/digital-news-report/2022/thailand","claim":"The report says self-censorship remained widely practised in mainstream Thai media, while student-led pro-democracy protests had helped open up media space and alternative social-media outlets that openly criticised the government and monarchy.","locator":"lines 35-37","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Expert-authored country chapter using survey and media-environment analysis; not a state source but methodologically grounded.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 media-environment evidence for the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Relevant to the information environment under Prayuth's government, though it does not attribute each media constraint to him personally.","contrary_evidence":["The same passage says self-censorship remained common, so the opening was partial.","It describes a broader media ecosystem rather than a single ruler decision."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.6","4B.10"]}
